# Scroll the Quran — service environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) only if a script or CI needs these. **The app does not read
# this file.** Nothing here is wired into the shipped app: it makes no network calls, and
# the RevenueCat and Supabase integrations are scaffolded, not live. See docs/infra/README.md.

# --- RevenueCat -------------------------------------------------------------
# The PUBLIC Apple SDK key (appl_…). Dashboard -> Project settings -> API keys.
# In the app this is not read from here — it goes in Config/Local.xcconfig as RC_API_KEY
# and reaches the bundle through App/Info.plist. This entry is for CI, which writes that
# xcconfig from a secret. See docs/infra/revenuecat.md.
RC_API_KEY=

# The SECRET key (sk_…) is for server calls only. It must never be in the app bundle, in
# web/, or in this file on a developer machine. Left here as a named absence on purpose.
# REVENUECAT_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Supabase ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API. The anon key is an RLS-scoped public JWT and is
# designed to ship in a client; it is still not committed, because rotating a key that is
# in git means rewriting history.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Bypasses every RLS policy in supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql. Server-side only.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Cloudflare -------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed for the documented flow: `npx wrangler login` uses a browser session, not a
# token. Only set these for unattended CI deploys of web/.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
